		(at 50.5 15 -90)
		(descr "CONSTRUCTED FOOTPRINT (see hardware/kicad/trace-dongle/generate_board.py report note): KiCad 10 std libs ship no ESP32-C3-MINI-1 footprint. Pad grid/courtyard/silkscreen below are copied verbatim from KiCad's own RF_Module:ESP32-C6-MINI-1 (same Espressif MINI-1 mechanical family; module body confirmed 13.2x16.6x2.4mm in BOTH the C6-MINI-1 footprint tags and the ESP32-C3-MINI-1 datasheet section 10 -- identical mechanical envelope/pad grid, 53 pads: 48 castellated I/O perimeter pads pitch 0.8mm + pad 49 center GND (8 sub-pads, thermal) + 4 corner GND pads 50-53). Pad ELECTRICAL FUNCTIONS below are remapped to the real ESP32-C3-MINI-1 pin table, extracted from the official datasheet PDF (Table 3-1 Pin Definitions, esp32-c3-mini-1_datasheet_en v2.2): GND=1,2,11,14,36-53; 3V3=3; EN=8; IO2=5; IO3=6; IO0=12; IO1=13; IO10=16; IO4=18; IO5=19; IO6=20; IO7=21; IO8=22; IO9=23; IO18=26; IO19=27; RXD0(GPIO20)=30; TXD0(GPIO21)=31; NC=4,7,9,10,15,17,24,25,28,29,32-35. No 3D model attached (none available for this constructed part).")
